            "reason": "semicolon",
            "scope": "economic_impact.body",
            "text": "Nonfarm-business productivity grew 2.1% and real output 2.3%, compared with 0.6% growth in real hourly compensation; unit labor costs rose 2.4%. These aggregates show continued gains in output per hour without a comparable increase in real pay, but they do not identify the source. Reuters reported that Federal Reserve official Jefferson said AI was boosting inflation and that its productivity effect may come in the future. His comment reinforces the need not to treat current aggregate productivity growth as evidence of a distinct AI contribution."
