            "reason": "semicolon",
            "scope": "macro.paragraphs[1]",
            "text": "The infrastructure pipeline is large, but projects and planned generation are not yet delivered capacity. Available records place 1,556 data-center sites in development, equal to 0.51 times the operating count. Commercial electricity demand is growing 3.5%, compared with 1.8% for total retail demand, and net planned generation additions through the pipeline horizon total 227.6 GW. Utility Dive reported that PJM was urged to delay a base-capacity auction until data centers were cut from its forecast. The request shows that large-load assumptions are consequential and disputed in grid planning; it does not establish that PJM\u2019s forecast is wrong."
